@@ -22733,3 +22733,22 @@ Dev Update | Patch 0289
 **Fixed with a small FIFO queue, not a rewrite.** New private `GameEngine.queuedResults: QuestResult[]` (transient, unsaved -- same "genuinely ephemeral" treatment `lastResult` itself already gets, explicitly not persisted). New `pushResult(result)` replaces every direct `this.lastResult = result` assignment: shows immediately if nothing's currently displayed (byte-identical to the old behavior for the single-completion case, the overwhelmingly common one), otherwise queues behind whatever's already showing. `dismissResult()` now drains the queue -- `this.lastResult = this.queuedResults.shift() ?? null` -- instead of just nulling out, so the next queued completion takes over the instant the player dismisses the current card, in the order they actually finished. `QuestResultCard` itself needed zero changes: it already keys off `result.questId` and re-mounts fresh per result, so handing it a new queued result through the exact same `lastResult` prop it already reads just works. `hardReset()` (new-guild wipe) also clears `queuedResults` alongside `lastResult`, so a fresh guild never inherits a stale queue from the guild it replaced.
 
 **Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean against a fresh clone with this patch applied. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- `queuedResults` is in-memory GameEngine state, not `GameState`, same as `lastResult` it sits beside. Worth a real playtest: send several heroes out at once on the same duration (Send All Idle onto freshly-refreshed boards is the easiest repro), let them all land in the same tick, and confirm every one of them gets its own reward card in turn rather than only the last.
+
+
+### Quest egg drop chance rebalanced 10x rarer (patch 0290)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Egg Drop Rebalance
+- Changed: quest egg drop odds cut to a tenth of what they were -- Easy 15% -> 1.5%, Normal 20% -> 2%, Hard 30% -> 3%, Epic 40% -> 4%, Legendary 50% -> 5%
+- Eggs are meant to be a rare find, not something most sessions produce several of -- same relative odds between difficulty tiers, just off a much rarer baseline
+```
+
+Direct request: reduce how often quests drop eggs, "very rare" as the target. Reported current values first, proposed a straight 10x-rarer cut preserving the existing shape (each difficulty tier still exactly 10x apart from the next), confirmed with the requester before implementing.
+
+**Current values were the patch 0280 fix, not the original design.** `pets.questEggDropChance.<difficulty>` (tuning.json) had been authored as a 0-1 fraction (0.15 for Easy, etc.) but `rng.chance()` reads its argument on a 0-100 scale like every other `*Chance`/`*Percent` entry in the table -- a 100x unit bug that made real drops 0.15% instead of the intended 15%. Patch 0280 fixed the unit bug, correctly restoring the *intended* 15/20/30/40/50% -- but at that rate, a session with several heroes cycling burst quests produced multiple eggs routinely, which reads as common, not rare, exactly the opposite of a hatchery pet's intended tone.
+
+**Rebalanced to 1.5/2/3/4/5%.** A flat 10x cut off the patch-0280 values, applied uniformly via `QuestManager.resolve`'s existing `rng.chance(questEggDropChance(quest.offer.difficulty))` roll (`pets.ts`) -- no code changed, tuning-only. Kept the exact same relative shape across difficulty (still precisely 10x apart step to step: Easy->Normal->Hard->Epic->Legendary) so harder content is still meaningfully better egg odds, just off a much rarer floor -- roughly one egg per 20-65 successful quests depending on difficulty, instead of one every 2-7. `tuning.json`'s `default` field updated alongside `value` for all five entries, matching this file's existing convention (every entry in the table currently has `value === default`; a deliberate rebalance moves both together rather than leaving a stale "reset" target behind). Descriptions appended (not rewritten) with the patch 0290 rationale, keeping patch 0280's own unit-bug history intact rather than erasing it.
+
+**Confirmed unaffected, explicitly out of scope:** raid egg drops (authored per-encounter in raid loot tables, not this flat-percentage system, so untouched) and chain-completion guaranteed eggs (`ChainDef.rewardEgg`, a fixed one-time grant on specific story beats, not a per-quest roll). Only the ordinary quest-board roll changed.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean against a fresh clone with this patch applied. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- tuning-data-only change, no `GameState` shape touched.
